This hosted adaptation uses the Sites Vinext starter, its existing framework,
authentication helpers and runtime build integration. Their existing notices
and dependency licenses remain applicable. Application-specific additions are
Guanying B2B workflows, evidence tracking, inquiry memory, HS search conditions,
D1 workspace isolation, encrypted per-account model configuration, and demo UI.
No Firecrawl paid API or upstream lead results are represented as connected here.

Vendored notices are retained in scripts/vite/sites-vite-plugin.LICENSE and
vendor/shadcn-tailwind-4.13.0.LICENSE.md. npm dependency licenses remain with
their packages. Public product/reference sources are identified in application
records. Public reference examples are not customer transaction data.
The screenshots added for publication show this application running locally
with an empty or explicitly synthetic workspace.
